# Electron Main Process

## Security defaults

```typescript
// BrowserWindow webPreferences
contextIsolation: true,
nodeIntegration: false,
sandbox: true,
```

- Expose APIs only through `contextBridge` in preload — never `remote`.
- **Renderer** loads Next.js: dev → `http://localhost:3000`; prod → static export from `out/index.html`.
- Do not use Next.js API routes for AW/LLM — keep those in main process.

## Responsibilities

| Process | Owns |
|---------|------|
| Main | BrowserWindow, Tray, Notification, AW HTTP, LLM calls, electron-store |
| Preload | Typed IPC bridge (`window.jerry.*`) |
| Renderer | UI state and user input only |

## macOS behavior

- Keep app running when all windows are closed (required for tray in v0.1).
- Use `app.dock.hide()` when running as menu-bar-only app (later tickets).

## IPC naming

- Channels: `jerry:<domain>:<action>` (e.g. `jerry:aw:getSnapshot`)
- Return `{ ok: true, data }` or `{ ok: false, error: string }` — avoid throwing across IPC.
